Debug logging (no behavior change) to empirically confirm/refute the
preemption-vs-offload-cascade race hypothesis from the 2026-08-21
conversation: a request preempted mid-prefill (before ever completing a
full turn) recomputes from scratch on retry -- Cached tokens: 0 (0.0%),
zero kv_offload_load activity -- even though the same offload tier
demonstrably restores multi-GB of KV cache correctly for requests that
finished normally and were evicted/resumed later (verified: real
kv_offload_load_bytes events, ~250ms for ~3GB, exactly matching
conversation-switch timestamps).

vLLM already has a purpose-built mechanism for this: a preempted
request's in-flight offload store jobs are supposed to be synchronously
flushed before its blocks can be reused (jobs_to_flush, built in
offloading/scheduler.py's build_connector_meta() and waited on in
offloading/worker.py's handle_preemptions()). Whether that flush
actually completes before the scheduler's own block-free
(_free_request_blocks() -> block_pool.py's free_blocks(), which only
returns a block to the reusable/cacheable pool once its ref_cnt reaches
exactly 0) is the open question -- this patch adds logger.debug() calls
at every step of that path so a live repro shows the actual order of
events:

  1. v1/core/sched/scheduler.py: _free_request_blocks() logs which path
     (immediate vs deferred) is taken for a preempted request, and the
     last_sched_seq/processed_step_seq values that decide it.
  2. v1/core/block_pool.py: free_blocks() logs any block whose ref_cnt
     doesn't reach 0 after decrementing -- the direct signal that
     something else (e.g. an in-flight offload cascade) still holds it.
  3. offloading/scheduler.py: build_connector_meta() logs when/whether
     jobs_to_flush actually gets populated for a preempted request.
  4. offloading/worker.py: handle_preemptions() logs before/after the
     synchronous wait() on those flushed jobs, with elapsed time.

All logger.debug() calls -- zero overhead unless debug logging is
enabled, no behavior change. Round-trip verified (apply/reverse/content
check) against vLLM 0.27.1.

--- a/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
+++ b/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
@@ -2342,11 +2342,24 @@
         """Free the request's KV blocks, deferring the return to the block
         pool when an in-flight GPU step may still write them.
         """
-        if not self.defer_block_free or (
+        immediate = not self.defer_block_free or (
             # Last scheduled step already processed: no in-flight write remains
             # (always the case for a normal finish), so free now.
             request.last_sched_seq <= self.processed_step_seq
-        ):
+        )
+        logger.debug(
+            "request-logging preemption-debug: _free_request_blocks(%s) "
+            "status=%s path=%s defer_block_free=%s last_sched_seq=%s "
+            "processed_step_seq=%s num_preemptions=%s",
+            request.request_id,
+            request.status,
+            "immediate" if immediate else "deferred",
+            self.defer_block_free,
+            request.last_sched_seq,
+            self.processed_step_seq,
+            request.num_preemptions,
+        )
+        if immediate:
             self.kv_cache_manager.free(request)
             return
         blocks = self.kv_cache_manager.pop_blocks_for_free(request)
--- a/v1/core/block_pool.py
+++ b/v1/core/block_pool.py
@@ -736,6 +736,16 @@
                     blocks_without_hash.append(block)
                 else:
                     blocks_with_hash.append(block)
+            elif block.ref_cnt > 0 and not block.is_null:
+                logger.debug(
+                    "request-logging preemption-debug: free_blocks() block %d "
+                    "NOT returned to cacheable pool (ref_cnt=%d after decrement, "
+                    "hash=%s) -- still held by another reference (e.g. an "
+                    "in-flight offload cascade)",
+                    block.block_id,
+                    block.ref_cnt,
+                    block.block_hash is not None,
+                )
 
         # Blocks without hash get evicted first - prepend them last to the tail
         self.free_block_queue.prepend_n(blocks_without_hash)
